-- Color.cm -- Gargoyle, the 1986 colour illustrator, on the colour display.-- Tim made his book's artwork in Gargoyle, so this is the tool, not a demo.Echo Turning the colour display on...ColorDisplay onEcho Fetching Gargoyle and its import closure. This is big; allow minutes.Bringover -p [Cedar]<CedarChest6.1>Top>Gargoyle.df-- BiScrollers, EXPLICITLY and from 6.1. This is why Gargoyle would not start.-- User.Profile loads BiScrollers from CedarChest6.0 at BOOT and Gargoyle is a-- 6.1 build, so Run Gargoyle.bcd dies on VersionMismatch[BiScrollers], no-- Gargoyle command is ever registered, and the .load file fails to register-- a command -- which is why there is no window and no other error.-- A plain Bringover, NOT -p: -p fetches public files only, and that is the-- likeliest reason the imported BiScrollers.df fetched nothing the first time.-- The profile is deliberately left alone: Sil is also a 6.0 build and imports-- SilBiScrollersImpl, so switching it wholesale would trade one working thing-- for another. Loading the newer version alongside is Cedar's own idiom.Echo Fetching the 6.1 BiScrollers Gargoyle was built against...Bringover -o Geom2DImpl.BCD BiScrollersImpl.BCD BiScrollersButtonned.BCD [Cedar]<CedarChest6.1>Top>BiScrollersEcho Loading it so Gargoyle can bind to it...Run Geom2DImpl BiScrollersImpl BiScrollersButtonnedEcho Loading Gargoyle, its packages, and the ColorTool...Source Gargoyle.loadEcho Now type  Gargoyle  to open it.